The unpredictable friction of millions of people going about their daily lives, the heat escaping from apartment windows, the exhaust from cars.

110
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:04,940
The sheer thermodynamic noise of reality.

111
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:08,340
It's a composite of mass, momentum, and heat.

112
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:10,020
All interacting at once.

113
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:19,240
Yeah, mathematically, the paper maps all three of these fields together into a single configuration space, ensuring they are always completely coupled.

114
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:26,360
A change in the vector flow of traffic will inevitably alter the entropy field through heat and friction.

115
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:31,980
But wait, if I'm building, say, an autonomous vehicle, I have a massive problem with this.

